# Mail fixtures are golden files for a package that compares bytes. Git's
# end-of-line conversion would rewrite them on checkout, so the same fixture
# would have different bytes on Windows than on macOS and a byte-level rule
# would mean something different per platform. -text pins them exactly as
# committed. The CRLF handling they exercise belongs in the test, not in the
# checkout.
*.eml -text
